{"id":"de4de360eb890a9eac474b351efd38802c875a46801afe635e3fe053f679a5a3","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-11-08T20:21:43.017996723Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## What to build\n\nFollow-up to 215ee3. `ti verify` reports parent/children and depends-on/blocks asymmetries; `ti verify --repair` fixes them. Authority rules to decide before building: the child's parent field is op-managed and wins for sub-issues; for dependencies both sides are sets, so the rule (union vs intersection, or newest tombstone wins) needs its own design pass. Dry-run by default, `--write` applies, idempotent, same shape as `ti migrate`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Design pass settles authority rules and records them in CONTEXT.md and the command help\n- [ ] `ti verify --repair` dry-run lists intended fixes; `--write` applies; second run is a no-op\n- [ ] CLI tests for each asymmetry kind"}}}